description:
Write file utilities with `java.nio.file`:

```java
// Summary.java
record Summary(int lines, int words, long characters, String longestLine) { }

// FileTools.java
class FileTools {
    static Summary summarize(Path file) throws IOException
    static int copyMatching(Path in, Path out, String needle) throws IOException
    static List<String> findByExtension(Path dir, String extension) throws IOException
}
```

- `summarize`: the number of lines, words (runs of non-white-space characters), characters (the file size in characters, line breaks included), and the longest line (the first one on a tie; `""` for an empty file).
- `copyMatching` writes the lines of `in` that contain `needle` (ignoring case) to `out`, creating missing parent directories, and returns how many lines it wrote. Read and write line by line with a `BufferedReader` and `BufferedWriter` in try-with-resources.
- `findByExtension` lists every regular file under `dir` (in subfolders too) whose name ends with `.` + `extension` (ignoring case), as paths relative to `dir` with `/` separators, sorted.

starter.FileTools.java:
